    {
      "source": "hn",
      "title": "Show HN: Ember – Redshift safe color palettes",
      "url": "https://github.com/carpdiem/ember",
      "author": "carpdiem",
      "byline": "carpdiem",
      "external_id": "49232870",
      "summary": null,
      "why_read": null,
      "authors": [],
      "category": null,
      "published": "2026-08-09T16:26:37Z",
      "score": 89,
      "comments": 19,
      "hn_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49232870",
      "points": 89,
      "num_comments": 19,
      "snippet": "Most color palettes collapse if you&#x27;ve got a strong redshift&#x2F;nightshift color filter actively suppressing green and blue channels. I made one that doesn&#x27;t.<p>Ember has terminal, chart, heatmap, and UI palettes designed and tested to be as distinguishable as possible under both the redshift &amp; non-redshift condition... so no more duplicate color appearances (or worse yet, disappearing colors!).",
      "links": []
    },
